msgid ""
"(filter) The questions about to be sent to the browser, after the questions "
"cache. Use it to localize or adjust the content. Never change the ids, their "
"order, the number of options or the \"answer\" index: scoring is done server-"
"side from the ids and the option indexes."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-developper.php:426
msgid ""
"(action) A question was added, updated or deleted from the admin screens."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-developper.php:430
msgid ""
"(action) Import of questions: all questions were deleted first (replace "
"mode; question ids change), then fired once after the questions were "
"inserted (not once per question). Questions inserted by the import do not "
"fire fqi3_question_created."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-developper.php:434
msgid ""
"(filter) The question rows returned by the REST endpoints /quizzes, /quizzes/"
"{id} and /quizzes/level/{name}, after the API cache. Do not change the ids, "
"the number of options or the \"answer\" index."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-developper.php:438
msgid ""
"(filter) Suffix added to the REST API cache keys. Return a stable value (for "
"example a language slug) when an add-on changes the content of a response "
"per request, so one variant is never served from another variant's cache "
"entry."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-developper.php:442
msgid ""
"(action) The core is loaded. Boot add-ons from here (or from plugins_loaded "
"at priority 10+): WordPress loads \"form-quizz-fqi3-xxx/\" plugins before "
"\"form-quizz-fqi3/\", so the core constants and classes do not exist while "
"an add-on main file is being included."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-developper.php:446
msgid ""
"(action) A server-side attempt was created. Fired once per attempt, for "
"logged-in users only. attempt_id is always greater than 0."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-developper.php:450
msgid ""
"(action) An attempt was completed. Fired exactly once per attempt, for "
"logged-in users only, after the server checked that its questions were "
"served, and with a score computed by the server from the submitted answers "
"(the score sent by the browser is ignored). attempt_id is always greater "
"than 0."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-developper.php:454
msgid ""
"(action) Before the results are displayed. Only trust it when $verified is "
"true (logged-in user: level and score recorded by the server). It is also "
"fired at page render with placeholder values and $verified = false, and for "
"visitors with browser-supplied values: never use an unverified call to grant "
"points, badges or data."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-developper.php:458
msgid ""
"(filter) Whether the current user may request the questions of a level. Runs "
"on every request: keep callbacks cheap (cached lookups, no remote call). The "
"core rules (levels flagged free for visitors) give the initial value; the "
"filter has the final say, so it can restrict a level or open it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/admin/class-developper.php:462
